{title: 160 - Ride On in Majesty}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #160 • CANNOCK • 8.9.7.8}
{lyricist: Henry H. Milman}
{composer: Walter K. Stanton}
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 160}
{meta: tune CANNOCK}
{meta: meter 8.9.7.8}
{meta: category Jesus Christ - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]Ride on! [C]ride [D]on [G/B]in [Am]majesty!
[G]Hark, [D/F#]all [Em]the [D/F#]tribes [Em]hosanna [D]cry;
[G7/F]O [C/E]Savior [Am]meek, [D]pursue [D7]Thy [Em]road
[Am]With [Bm/D]palms [D7/C]and [Bm]scattered [Am/C]garments [D]strowed.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]Ride on! [C]ride [D]on [G/B]in [Am]majesty!
[G]In [D/F#]lowly pomp [Bm]ride [Em]on [Am]to die;
[G7/F]O [C/E]Christ, [G/D]Thy [Am]triumphs [D]now [D7]begin
[Am]O'er [Bm/D]captive death [Em]and [Am/C]conquered [D]sin.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]Ride on! [C]ride [D]on [G/B]in [Am]majesty!
[G]The [D/F#]winged [Em]squadrons of [Am]the sky
[G7/F]Look [C/E]down [G/D]with [C]sad [Am]and [D]wondering [Em]eyes
[Am]To [Bm/D]see [D7/C]the [Bm]approaching [D]sacrifice.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[G]Ride on! [C]ride [D]on [G/B]in [Am]majesty!
[G]In [D/F#]lowly pomp [Bm]ride [Em]on [Am]to die;
[G7/F]Bow [C/E]Thy [G/D]meek [C]head [D]to [G/D]mortal [Em]pain,
[Am]Then [Bm/D]take, [D7/C]O [Bm]God, [Em]Thy [Am/C]power [D]and [G]reign.
{end_of_verse}
